1 1795385152 NOTE Owner ruling: checkpoint continuously so no work is lost if this box fails. Run bash $HOME/gate_wave.sh ckpt (a) right after the null control finishes, (b) right after each results/<key>.json write, (c) after every partial finding or mutant classification you record, and (d) at least every 10 minutes alongside the heartbeat while any uncheckpointed result exists. Write partial per-key notes to the wave dir as you go rather than holding them in context. Checkpoint failures go in the heartbeat, never a retry loop.
2 1795385386 NOTE Owner ruling: save every probe you write, not only results. gate_wave.sh ckpt copies only the wave dir, so a probe test or harness left only in your repo tree is lost if this box fails. Each time you write or edit a probe (a test file, harness, mutant driver or scratch script), copy it at once into the wave dir under probes/<key>/ keeping its repo-relative path (e.g. cp --parents from the tree root), plus a one-line probes/<key>/INDEX.md entry saying what it pins, then run bash $HOME/gate_wave.sh ckpt. On a re-fire, restore probes from probes/<key>/ before writing any new ones.
